<section class="how">
    <h2>How to Use This Tile Calculator</h2>
    <p>Installing floor or wall tiles requires calculating total coverage while factoring in edge cuts and grout lines. Use this tool with simple parameters:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Room Dimensions:</strong> Enter overall room length and width in feet or meters.</li>
        <li><strong>Tile Dimensions:</strong> Enter individual tile length and width in inches or centimeters (e.g., 12x12 inches or 30x30 cm).</li>
        <li><strong>Grout Joint Width:</strong> Standard grout line spacing ranges from 1/16 in (1.5 mm) for rectified tile up to 1/4 in (6 mm) for regular ceramic.</li>
        <li><strong>Waste Percentage:</strong> Standard straight installations require a 10% waste buffer. Diagonal layouts or complex rooms with obstacles require 15%.</li>
    </ul>
</section>

<section class="formula">
    <h2>Tile Coverage Formulas & Grout Calculations</h2>
    <p>Calculating tile quantities requires converting room dimensions and tile dimensions into identical unit metrics before applying waste multipliers:</p>
    
    <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; margin: 1.5rem 0;">
        <div style="background: var(--input-bg); padding: 1.25rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid var(--border);">
            <h3 style="margin-top: 0; font-size: 1.1rem; color: #2563eb;">Single Tile Area Formula</h3>
            <p style="font-size: 0.9rem;">Includes individual tile dimensions plus grout joint width:</p>
            <p><code>Effective Area = (Length + Grout) x (Width + Grout)</code></p>
        </div>

        <div style="background: var(--input-bg); padding: 1.25rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid var(--border);">
            <h3 style="margin-top: 0; font-size: 1.1rem; color: #7c3aed;">Total Tiles & Box Count Formula</h3>
            <p style="font-size: 0.9rem;">Total net tiles required multiplied by cutting waste factor:</p>
            <p><code>Total Tiles = (Floor Area / Tile Area) x (1 + Waste %)</code></p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

