<section class="faq">
    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

    <h3>Why do I need to calculate a tile waste percentage?</h3>
    <p>Cutting tiles to fit room edges, plumbing pipes, and corners leaves unusable tile remnants. Standard straight layouts require 10 percent waste, while diagonal patterns require 15 percent extra tile volume.</p>

    <h3>How does grout line width affect total tile count?</h3>
    <p>Wider grout lines slightly increase the overall coverage area of each tile, reducing total raw tile count marginally. However, grout joint spacing is primarily calculated to ensure straight, professional installations.</p>

    <h3>How many extra tiles should I keep after installation?</h3>
    <p>Keeping at least one full box of extra tiles ensures exact dye-lot color matching for future repairs if tiles crack or chip over time.</p>

    <h3>Can I use this calculator for wall tiles and backsplashes?</h3>
    <p>Yes. Enter the total height and width of your wall or kitchen backsplash area into the room length and width fields to calculate wall tile coverage accurately.</p>
